rem === Basic SETERR Error Trapping ===
rem Demonstrates: SETERR + label pattern; execution branches to handler on error
rem Expected output: Error # 41  -  Invalid assignment

seterr handler

rem Attempt to convert a non-numeric string to a number
x = num("not a number")
print "This line is never reached"
release

handler:
    print "Error #", err, " - ", errmes(-1)
    release
